## Prerequisites

- the shared infrastructure installed on the cluster — `prod_common_DNS-01`
  or `prod_common_HTTP-01` — providing the Gateway `[[ gateway_name ]]`, its
  certificate and the shared http→https redirect;
- `[[ hostname ]]` resolving to the Gateway IP — covered already if the zone
  has a wildcard `A` record, otherwise create one:
  `kubectl get gateway [[ gateway_name ]] -n [[ gateway_namespace ]] -o jsonpath='{.status.addresses[0].value}'`;
- `$REGISTRY_TOKEN` exported, with `write:packages` locally and
  `read:packages` for the cluster;
- `just`, `podman` (or `CONTAINER_ENGINE=docker`), `kubectl`.

## First deploy

```shell
export REGISTRY_TOKEN=ghp_...
just login
just release          # build + push both images at [[ version ]]
just bootstrap        # namespace + pull Secret
just deploy
just smoke
```

`just bootstrap` prints a reminder to check that the namespace carries
`gateway-access=true`; without it the HTTPRoute is rejected by the Gateway.
The cluster operator grants it with `just grant [[ namespace ]]` from the
shared infrastructure directory. On an HTTP-01 cluster that directory must
also have a listener named `[[ gateway_listener ]]` for this hostname.

## Ship a new version

```shell
just bump 0.2.0       # rewrites the tag here and in both Deployments
just release
just deploy
just smoke
```

Never overwrite a tag that has been pushed. `just undo backend` rolls one
component back.

## Day to day

```shell
just status
just logs-backend
just route            # Accepted / ResolvedRefs conditions
just events
just scale backend 4
```

| Symptom | Cause |
| --- | --- |
| `404` with nginx HTML on `[[ api_prefix ]]/` | the API rule did not match — check `value: [[ api_prefix ]]` in `kubernetes/http-route.yml` |
| `404` with `{"detail":"Not Found"}` | the `URLRewrite` filter is missing; the backend only serves `/` |
| `503` | no ready backend endpoint — `just endpoints`, `just logs-backend` |
| `404` from Envoy for everything | no DNS record, or the route is not `Accepted` — `just route` |
| Route `Accepted=False` | the namespace lacks `gateway-access=true`, or a wrong `sectionName` |
| `ImagePullBackOff` | `just create-pull-secret` (it is namespaced), or the tag was never pushed |
| Pods `Running` but `0/1 READY` | readiness probe — `kubectl describe pod -n [[ namespace ]]` |
| frontend crashes at startup, read-only filesystem error | a `docker-entrypoint.d` script wants a path not backed by an `emptyDir`; add the mount, or set `readOnlyRootFilesystem: false` for that container |

## Notes

- **`--root-path [[ api_prefix ]]`** in `kubernetes/backend/deployment.yml` is
  the counterpart of the `URLRewrite` filter in the route: the Gateway strips
  the prefix, uvicorn puts it back into generated URLs so `/docs` works.
  Removing one without the other returns a flat `404`.
- Both containers run **non-root with a read-only root filesystem**; anything
  written at runtime goes to an `emptyDir`.
- Local run: `just run-backend`, `just run-frontend` (8000 and 8080).

